-- The other CONSIDERs whose every WHEN is one condition: one that lists every
-- option and has no OTHERWISE, one over numbers, one in a rule that answers
-- TRUE or FALSE, and one with an EXACTLY arm (smucclaw/l4-ide#1094).
DECLARE Plan IS ONE OF basic, pro, team

-- Every option is listed, so no plan is none of them, and the solver proves
-- that combination impossible.
GIVEN p IS A Plan
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `fee for every plan` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN basic THEN 5
    WHEN pro THEN 20
    WHEN team THEN 50

GIVEN seats IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `fee for seats` seats IS
    CONSIDER seats
    WHEN 1 THEN 5
    WHEN 2 THEN 9
    OTHERWISE 20

GIVEN p IS A Plan
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is billed monthly` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN basic THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- An EXACTLY arm is the condition that the scrutinee equals its value, here
-- another input, so the seats at the cap are free whatever the cap is.
GIVEN seats IS A NUMBER, cap IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `fee up to the cap` seats cap IS
    CONSIDER seats
    WHEN EXACTLY cap THEN 0
    WHEN 1 THEN 5
    OTHERWISE 20
